# Security by design

- Default deny. Fail closed when policy is missing or ambiguous.
- No backend route without centralized authentication and authorization unless explicitly marked public in the typed route registry.
- No ad hoc / route-level permission checks. Use centralized typed permissions and scopes.
- No secrets or PII leakage in logs, errors, traces, prompts, or Langfuse metadata.
- Validate all trust boundaries at runtime (HTTP, queue, agent, file, env).
- Never rely on frontend authorization as a security control.
- Never decode JWTs without full validation for authorization decisions.

